From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:45:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the database export, the Xiaomi music snapshot and time
 sync, and keep every sheet below the status bar

Database export:
- Export to a temporary file first, check the SQLite header, and only then
  write the target, so a failing run can no longer truncate the previous backup.
- A missing export location is reported instead of silently succeeding.

Xiaomi music:
- Send a complete snapshot (state, track, artist, position, duration) on every
  metadata or playback-state change, but only when that part actually changed,
  instead of flooding the link with identical packets.
- Keep the newest metadata and playback state across the debounce, so a
  state-only callback no longer replaces a pending metadata update with null;
  metadata updates no longer reset the cached playback state and position, and
  forwarding is skipped while the device service is unavailable.
- Map the playback state to the wire values the watch expects and keep the
  track when only the playback state changes.

Xiaomi time sync:
- Re-send the clock once per connection after the watch answers a device state
  request, and add an explicit syncNow entry point.

Backup on app open:
- Give the feature its own settings section, keep the folder row tappable, add
  a reset-to-default action, and make a blank location fall back to the default.

Settings UI:
- GbSettingRow now attaches its onClick, so every Compose settings row works.
- PrefsRefresh lets a fragment invalidate the Compose renderer when it replaces
  a summary without writing a preference (worker status, last run).

Sleep chart:
- Space the value and the score line inside the ring and shrink the line when
  it would touch the stroke; localize it with the current context.
- Show a hint under the ring that opens the score breakdown.

Sheets:
- Cap Compose and View bottom sheets below the status bar so they no longer
  cover the punch-hole camera.
